(a) Generally. All commercial and industrial generators of solid waste within the city are responsible for assuring the safe handling, storage and collection of waste from their premises in accordance with the most recent franchise agreement. The city sanitation department or contract hauler can provide regularly scheduled collection and handling services for all commercial and industrial customers, except for the handling of hazardous constituents.
(b) Special waste handling. The generator of any special waste shall be responsible for disposing of the special waste in accordance with all state and federal laws.
(c) Prohibited wastes. The sanitation department or designee shall not empty a commercial refuse container that contains any of the following items:
(1) Scrap tires and heavy motor vehicle parts such as engines and transmissions;
(2) Liquids, including paint, cooking oil and motor vehicle fluids and lubricants;
(3) Logs or limbs over four feet in length or four inches in diameter;
(4) Rocks, dirt, bricks, concrete, stone, plaster, sheetrock, roofing or other similar materials;
(5) Uncontainerized refuse, such as lumber that protrudes from the container or refuse placed on top or in front of the container;
(6) Any acid, explosive material, inflammable liquids, dangerous or corrosive material of any kind, including lead-acid vehicle batteries;
(7) Yard trimmings;
(8) Any other material prohibited by state or federal law.
(Code 1993, pt. II, § 74-37; Ord. No. 12202012-1, 12-20-2012)

